# The repo has core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites line endings in anything Git classifies as
# text. Classification is a content heuristic, and the icons are the files where a wrong guess is
# unrecoverable: a single 0x0A turned into 0x0D0A inside an .ico or .icns corrupts it silently —
# it still commits, still checks out, and simply stops being a valid icon. Declaring the binary
# types removes the guess.
#
# Deliberately NOT declaring `* text=auto` here: that would renormalise every existing source
# file in the tree at once, which is a whole-repo change that deserves its own commit rather than
# riding along inside an unrelated one.

*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.gif binary
*.mp4 binary
*.mov binary
*.wav binary
*.opencut binary

# Vectors and source are text, and should be LF everywhere so the icon pipeline's output is
# byte-identical no matter which platform ran it.
*.svg text eol=lf
